From 95f83d0d214843a67fd6238a7923c8c69d56fa88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:37:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(asks): a goal stopped mid-send sends nothing (P1, the
 tester's 48089)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Conv 46897: „შეაჩერე ეს მიზანი." closed goal 22773 at 03:14:17 and the reply
said nothing more would go — yet the day-one run already inside createAsk
wrote asks 17822 and 17823 at 03:14:24 and 03:14:26. Not a cache: createAsk
read the goal's status once, at its top, and the editor's model call and the
rest take seconds before the message is written.

The goal is now read again, fresh, at the two points that matter: before the
reader's conversation is opened, and right before the message is written.
After the insert it is read once more; if a stop slipped into that last
moment, the stop's own cancelAsksForTask runs again, so the reader is told
and nothing stays „sent" on a closed goal. A failed re-read refuses: a stop
holds even when the database is slow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
